  "question": {
    "text": "The line $y-\\sqrt{3} x+3=0$ cuts the parabola $y^2=x+2$ at the points $P$ and $Q$. If the co-ordinates of the point $X$ are $(\\sqrt{3}, 0)$, then the value of $X P \\cdot X Q$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "YJ2cV",
      "text": "$\\frac{4(2+\\sqrt{3})}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "iv59j",
      "text": "$\\frac{4(2-\\sqrt{3})}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1JDtH",
      "text": "$\\frac{5(2+\\sqrt{3})}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "K8BFX",
      "text": "$\\frac{5(2-\\sqrt{3})}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Arbitrary point on the line $\\left(\\sqrt{3}+\\frac{r}{2}, \\frac{r \\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)$ satisfying in the parabola $\\Rightarrow 3 r^2-2 r-(4 \\sqrt{3}+8)=0$\n$\\because$ roots $r_1$ & $r_2$\n$\\therefore$ product $r_1 r_2=-\\frac{4 \\sqrt{3}+8}{3}$\n$\\therefore X P \\cdot X Q=\\left|r_1 r_2\\right|=\\frac{4}{3}(\\sqrt{3}+2)$",
    "image": null
  },
